1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
UptimeBuyer: commercial-refrigeration recovery with cited evidence and bounded spending. SERV Hackathon 02, Kite track.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
SERV Reasoning reads the manual and proposes cited facts and candidate actions. A proposal has no authority.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Deterministic code decides compatibility, safety and budget. A separate broker is the only process that can pay.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
SIMULATED: the local demo stack. SIMULATOR sensors, a recorded-contract broker, contract-fake reasoning and CMMS, synthetic data.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
SIMULATED: a temperature breach opens one incident, with its deadline and the next safe action.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
SIMULATED: cited facts from synthetic documents. In this part the reasoning adapter is a contract fake.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
SIMULATED: code decides compatibility (ALLOW, HOLD or REJECT). The approval bounds amount, merchant and expiry.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
SIMULATED: a recorded-contract broker, not Kite, reports this session and order. No money moves in this part.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
SIMULATED: an ambiguous payment outcome stays UNKNOWN and is reconciled before any retry.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
SIMULATED: a provider saying "done" cannot close the incident. It needs a stable sensor window and a sign-off.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
SIMULATED: every decision, approval and external attempt lands in the append-only ledger.

12
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
REAL EVIDENCE: one SERV Reasoning run (serv-mini) over the published Dixell XR60CX manual. Cost $0.024365.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The product re-opened all 7 citations against the stored manual and accepted the proposal. It carries no authority.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Journey gate: document PASS and reasoning PASS. Sensor, payment, recovery and timeout in this journey: NOT_RUN.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
The run before it was REJECTED by the citation validator; the PDF font decoding was fixed and the run repeated.

16
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:56,000
REAL EVIDENCE: under a signed owner authorization, the broker made one 0.01 USDC x402 payment through Kite Passport.

17
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,000
The Kite spending session was approved with a passkey and capped at one cent per call and in total.

18
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:10,000
lionx402.com answered HTTP 200 with 7 refrigeration-repair businesses. A duplicate request caused no second charge.

19
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,000
kpass reported settlement chain 2366, not Base (8453), so the broker recorded UNKNOWN and did not retry.

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:25,000
The owner resolved it CAPTURED from out-of-band evidence: wallet 1.10 to 1.09 USDC, Kite activity, session spent 0.01.

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
What chain 2366 denotes is still an open question for Kite.

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Journey gate: payment, fulfillment and duplicate PASS. Sensor, recovery and timeout: NOT_RUN.

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Not yet proven: a physical sensor, physical recovery evidence, the timeout case and a hosted deployment. All NOT_RUN.

24
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
No single run has passed every part yet, so the complete real-input journey (T-058) is NOT_RUN.

25
